    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its cases (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner response. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by a MapStruct mapper, the change is three small edits following the existing pattern used for `membershipLevel` and `locality`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema as a read-only enum (`EMAIL` / `PHONE`), which generates `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small derivation helper mirroring `MembershipLevel`: returns `EMAIL` when `owner.getEmail()` is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `PHONE`.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression wiring `contactPreference` to `ContactPreference.of(owner)`, so every owner DTO (GET, create, update, list) carries the derived value.\n\nBecause the rule sits on the shared mapper, it applies consistently across all owner responses, not just the `GET /api/owners/{id}` path the tests exercise.",
